==============================================================================
 ZXMetalCircle - cmdline.txt options
==============================================================================

(English version of cmdline.hlp.)

Every option (except logdev) can also be changed from the emulator: F1 and
then C (settings). G saves them here (a copy is left in cmdline.bak).

If an option is misspelt, the emulator says so at boot for about 10 seconds
(for example "sounddev=sndpwn not valid") and uses the default value.

 cmdline.txt must have ALL the options on A SINGLE LINE, separated by
 spaces, without comments. This file only explains the options; the
 emulator does not read it. An option that is not there uses its default.

 Example:
   model=128k tape=flash joystick=kempston sounddev=sndhdmi net=auto tz=0 lang=en

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 MACHINE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 model=128k       Model at boot (F7 changes it on the fly):
                    16k     ZX Spectrum 16K
                    48k     ZX Spectrum 48K
                    128k    ZX Spectrum 128K                (default)
                    plus2   ZX Spectrum +2 (grey)
                    plus2a  ZX Spectrum +2A
                    plus3   ZX Spectrum +3 (with disk drive, .DSK disks)
                    plus3e  ZX Spectrum +3e (the +3 with Garry Lancaster's
                            ROMs and a hard disk on a ZXMMC card)

 lang=es          Language of the menus and the web page: es (Spanish) or
                  en (English), or any other in the locales folder. Also
                  changed in the settings (F1 and then C).

 p3elang=es       Language of the included +3e ROMs:  es  or  en

 hdd=             +3e hard disk image mounted at boot (switches to the
                  +3e). Path inside the SD card, for example:
                    hdd=hdd/marocana.vhd
                  Formats: .vhd .img .raw .hdf. It can also be chosen in
                  the settings (F1, C: "Boot hard disk"), and for the
                  session it is mounted from the browser, the drives
                  screen (Alt+U) or with "load" in the web page.
                  hdd=none: none.

 rom48=  rom128=  romplus2=  romplus2a=  romplus3=  romplus3e=  romif1=
                  (default = the usual one; also in the settings, page 7
                  "ROMs and folders")
                  Another file name (in the roms folder of the SD card) for
                  each machine's ROM or the Interface 1's. Without the
                  option, 48.rom, 128.rom, plus2.rom, plus2a.rom, plus3.rom,
                  plus3e.rom (or plus3e-es.rom / plus3e-en.rom) and if1.rom
                  are used. Only the 48K and 128K have their ROM inside the
                  emulator: if another machine's ROM is missing, that
                  machine is not available (see roms/README.txt).
                  Example: romplus3e=zxp3.rom

 issue=3          16K/48K keyboard board (also in F1, C):
                    3   Issue 3 (default)
                    2   Issue 2 (some old programs need it)

 speed=1          Emulation speed at boot (F10 changes it):
                    1, 2, 4 or 10 (x1 = real speed; faster ones are silent)

 ulaplus=1        ULAplus (64 colours):  1 = available,  0 = disabled

 rs232=1          Interface 1 RS232 on the Pi's TCP port 2323 (or to
                  saves/rs232.txt if nobody is connected). 0 = off.

 zxnet=1          Interface 1 ZX Net network between Pis on the local
                  network (UDP 5050, by broadcast). 0 = off.

 lec=0            528 KB LEC memory expansion (48K; on the 128K models,
                  from 48 BASIC), needed for LEC's CP/M (Alt+L connects
                  it on the fly):
                    0 = no (default),  1 = connected

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 TAPE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 tape=flash       Loading mode (F6 changes it on the fly):
                    flash   instant (standard blocks at once)  (default)
                    fast    fast, the loading can be seen
                    normal  real, at the speed of a Spectrum

 tapeaccel=1      Accelerate loaders (as in Fuse), in fast and instant
                  loading: if the loop that waits for each tape edge is a
                  known one (the ROM and its copies, Alkatraz, Microprose,
                  Digital Integration...), the wait is skipped in the data.
                  It also works with many turbo loaders. 0 = no (if a game
                  fails to load)

 tapesound=1      Hear the tape signal while loading: 1 = yes, 0 = no

 savetrap=1       The ROM's SAVE writes straight to the SD card (saves
                  folder):  1 = yes (default),  0 = no

 savefmt=tap      Format of SAVE recordings:  tap  or  tzx

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SNAPSHOTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 snapformat=z80   Format when saving with F8 (snaps folder):
                    z80  (default),  sna  or  szx

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 KEYBOARD, JOYSTICK AND MOUSE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 joystick=kempston  Emulated joystick (F4 changes it on the fly):
                    none       none
                    kempston   Kempston                        (default)
                    fuller     Fuller
                    sinclair1  Sinclair 1 (Interface 2, keys 6-0)
                    sinclair2  Sinclair 2 (Interface 2, keys 1-5)
                    cursor     Cursor / AGF / Protek (keys 5-8 and 0)
                    qaop       Q A O P and space

 cursors=both     What the PC keyboard's cursor keys do:
                    both      Spectrum cursor keys (CAPS SHIFT+5-8)
                              and also the joystick            (default)
                    keys      Spectrum cursor keys only
                    joystick  joystick only

 recreated=auto   Recreated ZX Spectrum keyboard (Elite) in "Layer A":
                    0     there is none: normal keyboard without delay
                    auto  automatic detection (default); through a USB
                          cable it is recognised when connected (0F39:0404)
                    1     every USB keyboard is a Recreated

 gpiokbd=48       Real Spectrum keyboard (and joysticks) through GPIO,
                  pastbytes' wiring (see README):
                    48     8 x 5 keyboards: 48K, Spectrum+, 128 and grey +2
                           (default; 1 or 128 also work)
                    plus3  +2A/+2B/+3 keyboard (13 x 11, 11 more pins).
                           Uses GPIO21, 16 and 12: no extended mode or NMI
                           buttons, and no gpioaudio. The tape input
                           (ear=gpio) then goes through GPIO15
                    0      no GPIO keyboard (leaves the pins free)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SOUND
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 sounddev=sndhdmi Sound output:
                    sndhdmi  through HDMI                    (default)
                             (on the Pi 4 and Pi 5, HDMI0 only: the
                             connector next to the power input)
                    sndpwm   through the 3.5 mm jack (Pi 1-4); on the Pi 5,
                             through GPIO12 and GPIO13 (only with gpiokbd=0,
                             as they are GPIO keyboard lines)
                    sndusb   USB sound card (Pi 4/400 and Pi 5/500; with
                             ear=usb it uses the same card)
                    none     no sound

 gpioaudio=1      With sounddev=sndpwm, also output the sound on GPIO12
                  (pin 32, mono):  1 = yes,  0 = no

 speaker=auto     Speaker model for the beeper (as in Fuse): auto (48K =
                  internal speaker, 128K/+2/+3 = television), beeper, tv
                  or off

 beeperfilter=1   Beeper low-pass filter, like the real speaker (removes
                  the whine of 1-bit carriers). 0 = no filter

 aystereo=abc     AY chip stereo layout (F9 changes it on the fly):
                    abc  (default),  acb,  bac  or  mono

 ear=0            Tape input from a real cassette (see README):
                    0     no input (default)
                    gpio  through a GPIO, with an LM393 comparator
                    usb   input of a USB sound card (Pi 4/400)
                  Alt+G records the input to saves/rec_NNN.tzx

 earpin=20        GPIO (BCM number) of the input with ear=gpio. Default
                  20 (pin 38); with gpiokbd=plus3, 15 (pin 10), the serial
                  port's RX (logging through the serial port keeps
                  working: it only uses TX, GPIO14). If the GPIO is already
                  used for something else, the input is not enabled

 earinvert=0      1 if the comparator's signal arrives inverted

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 IMAGE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 border=full      Border size (Alt+B changes it on the fly):
                    none      no border              (256 x 192)
                    standard  standard               (320 x 240)
                    full      full                   (352 x 296, default)
                    huge      huge                   (384 x 304)

 scanlines=0      TV scanlines (Alt+S):  1 = yes,  0 = no

 multicore=1      Pi 2, 3, 4 and Zero 2 W: the image scaling runs on core 1
                  (0 = everything on core 0)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 PERIPHERALS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 multiface=1      Multiface One/128/3 on F5 (needs its ROMs in the roms
                  folder of the SD card):  1 = yes,  0 = no

 divmmc=0         divMMC with esxDOS:
                    0       no divMMC (default)
                    esxdos  divMMC with esxDOS 0.8.9; its card is the
                            hdd/esxdos.img image (see esxdir=).
                            It cannot be used with the Interface 1, the
                            LEC memory or the Multiface
                  F5 opens the esxDOS browser. It is also connected or
                  disconnected with Alt+X or in the settings (F1, C,
                  page 5).

 esxdir=esxdos_i  SD card folder whose contents are copied to the esxDOS
                  card (hdd/esxdos.img) and deleted from the folder.
                  0 = do not import anything.

 romesx=          Another esxDOS ROM in the roms folder (default
                  esxmmc.bin, 8192 bytes)

 spectranet=0     Spectranet network card (1 = on). It uses the Pi's
                  network; F5 opens its menu. It cannot be used with the
                  divMMC, the Interface 1 or the Multiface. Its flash is
                  saved in spectranet.flash (in the root of the SD card).
                  It is also connected or disconnected with Alt+T or in
                  the settings (F1, C, page 5).

 romsnet=         Another initial Spectranet flash in the roms folder
                  (default spectranet.rom, 131072 bytes)

 if1=auto         Interface 1 with microdrives:
                    auto  connects when a cartridge is inserted (default)
                    1     always connected
                    0     never

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 NETWORK (WiFi or cable)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 net=auto         Network:
                    auto  WiFi if wpa_supplicant.conf exists and the model
                          has WiFi; otherwise cable         (default)
                    wifi  WiFi only
                    eth   cable only (or USB network adapter)
                    0     no network

 tz=60            Offset from universal time, in MINUTES (without summer
                  time):
                    60    mainland Spain and Balearic Islands  (default)
                    0     Canary Islands, Portugal, United Kingdom
                    -300  New York (a sign is allowed)

 dst=1            Automatic European summer time: 1 = yes, 0 = no

 tlsverify=1      HTTPS downloads (web page search): check the server's
                  certificate against certs/cacert.pem
                    1  yes (default)
                    0  no (only if it fails because of a certificate and
                       you trust the network)

 web=1            The emulator's web page:
                    1   full (default)
                    ro  read-only: browse, download and load; no uploads,
                        deletes, new folders or ZXDB downloads
                    0   off

 webpass=         Web page password (empty = no password). It is asked
                  once; it is not encrypted: it protects you on your local
                  network, not from someone eavesdropping

 ip=              Fixed IP. Without it, DHCP is used (the normal case).
 mask=            Network mask          (default 255.255.255.0)
 gw=              Gateway               (default the network's .1)
 dns=             DNS server            (default the gateway)
                  Example: ip=192.168.1.50 gw=192.168.1.1 dns=8.8.8.8

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SYSTEM (Circle options)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 logdev=ttyS1     Diagnostic messages through the serial port (GPIO14/15,
                  115200 baud). Only useful for debugging.

==============================================================================
 The WiFi settings go separately, in wpa_supplicant.conf (see
 wpa_supplicant.conf.ejemplo). The function keys are in the help (F1).
==============================================================================
